From: Lưu Oa Oa <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Route the m17n IME extension to the native mojo engine (step 0)

Make ash route the m17n input-method extension through NativeInputMethodEngine
so the first-party mojo IME path (and the UnikeyEngine behind it) actually
serves physical Vietnamese keystrokes, instead of the keys being handled
entirely in the component extension's JavaScript. This is the real step-0
routing fix; it supersedes an earlier throwaway observer-side probe.
diff --git a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/input_ime/input_ime_api_chromeos.cc b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/input_ime/input_ime_api_chromeos.cc
index 694d324f88..d9845de187 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/input_ime/input_ime_api_chromeos.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/input_ime/input_ime_api_chromeos.cc
@@ -911,8 +911,27 @@ bool InputImeEventRouter::RegisterImeExtension(
   }
 
   auto observer = std::make_unique<ImeObserverChromeOS>(extension_id, profile);
+  // Only the first-party input-method component extension is backed by the
+  // native (mojo + IME service) engine; every other extension gets the plain
+  // extension-hosted engine.
+  //
+  // On official Google Chrome builds a single component extension
+  // ("jkghodnilhceideoidjikpgommlajknk") hosts XKB, m17n, Mozc, Pinyin, ... and
+  // kM17nExtensionId is that same id, so this check is unchanged there. On
+  // unbranded ChromiumOS/colorburst builds the m17n rule-based layouts
+  // (vkd_*, including vkd_vi_telex/vkd_vi_vni) live in their *own* extension
+  // (kM17nExtensionId == "jhffeifommiaekmbkkjlpmilogcfdohp"), which previously
+  // fell through to the plain InputMethodEngine. That is why physical
+  // Vietnamese typing was served entirely by the extension's JavaScript and the
+  // C++ mojo path (NativeInputMethodEngineObserver -> ConnectToImeService ->
+  // the sandboxed IME service) never ran. Routing the m17n extension through
+  // NativeInputMethodEngine lets OnActivate() reach ConnectToImeService() for
+  // the vkd_* rule-based family and spawn the IME service. See
+  // internal-knowledge/VIETNAMESE-IME-PERF.md.
+  const bool is_native_ime_extension =
+      extension_id == ash::extension_ime_util::kM17nExtensionId;
   auto engine =
-      extension_id == "jkghodnilhceideoidjikpgommlajknk"
+      is_native_ime_extension
           ? std::make_unique<ash::input_method::NativeInputMethodEngine>()
           : std::make_unique<InputMethodEngine>();
   engine->Initialize(std::move(observer), extension_id.c_str(), profile);
